  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MR3: Mersin CNG Bus Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project supported Mersin Metropolitan Municipality through a EUR 15 million  senior unsecured EBRD loan and a EUR 7 million investment grant from the EBRD  Shareholder Special Fund (&quot;SSF&quot;) to modernise and expand its public transport  network. The Project ultimately financed the procurement of 118 CNG buses,  exceeding the original target of 100 buses as a result of favourable  procurement outcomes. The buses have been delivered and operational since 2022.  The proceeds of the loan and the capex grants were utilised to finance the  procurement of 118 new CNG powered buses (Euro 6 standard). The Project  expanded the urban transport capacity in Mersin and relieved pressure on  existing municipal services by providing extra capacity and better quality  services. By virtue of this investment, the average vehicle age of the bus  fleet of the City was reduced by: (i) the replacement of 44 ageing diesel buses  (Euro 1 standard, 1990-99 model) that were experiencing frequent breakdowns;  and (ii) the addition of 74 new CNG buses that expanded the fleet and enhanced  service coverage and capacity across the network.</narrative>
  </description>
